<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Cossacks</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Cossack</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Cossacks were self-governing communities of warriors in the steppe borderlands of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ukraine">Ukraine</a> and southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russia">Russia</a>. In the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/polish-lithuanian-commonwealth">Polish-Lithuanian Commonwealth</a>, the uprising led by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bohdan-khmelnytsky">Bohdan Khmelnytsky</a> from 1648 caused catastrophic losses. In the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russian-empire">Russian Empire</a>, Cossack hosts served as frontier troops and played a major part in expansion into <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/siberia">Siberia</a>.</p></div>
